<title>PHILIPPINES: Samanda banking unit resources grow in 96.</title>
<headline>Samanda banking unit resources grow in 96.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westmont Bank, an affiliate of Samanda Holdings Bhd, said on Friday the bank's total resources grew by 38 percent last year to 17.8 billion pesos from 12.9 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Total deposits rose by 41 percent to 14.4 billion pesos, while loan portfolio rose by 56 percent to 13.3 billion pesos, bank president Edgardo Espiritu said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank did not disclose its net income for the year.</p>
<p>Westmont attributed the growth to the expansion of its branch network to 73 from 33 branches in 1994.</p>
<p>Samanda is a member of the Westmont Group of Malaysia.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
